  message: "CORRECTION-OF-CORRECTION (2026-07-14, PR #640, dev @ c0a40ff689). Fresh adversarial re-verification (2 independent code-reading agents) OVERTURNED two claims in my earlier 2026-07-14 RECORD-CORRECTION on this item:\n\n(1) \"WI-tanot Category B (the _analyzer phantoms) is a delicate, not-minimally-reproducible INV-fahub fix\" — FALSE. It is CHEAP and minimally reproducible; now FIXED (PR #640), and Category B is fully closed. My earlier \"could not reproduce\" used the wrong shape (a single method `from pkg import sub as m; m._analyzer`, which emits NO edge — from-imports go to symbol_imports, so the module_attr_ref gate misses); the real trigger needs a SIBLING scope's plain `import pkg.sub as m` polluting the FILE-scoped module_imports. Fix = exclude co-referent from-import module aliases from the INV-fahub shadow set (~15 lines, per-alias exact). NO global cross-package map was needed — my 2026-07-13 \"architectural\" framing (and its restatement in the RECORD-CORRECTION) was wrong. Full mechanism + evidence on WI-tanot.\n\n(2) \"Category D is a verified ADR-0041 §3 + ADR-0037 double violation\" — FALSE. ADR-0041 EXPLICITLY scopes INV-nuzas out and accepts phantom workspace twins as tier-3 externals \"until the workspace-resolution fix lands\"; there is no \"tier=stdlib\" (stdlib = tier-3 + ecosystem axis), so the phantom's tier is correct and is_stdlib_module correctly returns False on the garbage workspace input. ADR-0037 governs resolution-STATE coherence (is_resolved=False + populated dst_ref = coherent \"identified external\" cell), NOT module-name accuracy. Category D is a REAL INV-nuzas bug but NOT an ADR violation. Also: phantom #3 (serve._ws_clients:copy) is set.copy() — a builtin METHOD, not the stdlib copy MODULE. Corrected D mechanism + fix shape recorded on WI-tanot.\n\nAlso corrected: the \"build a global module_to_file_id\" framing was stale — that map is already built global whole-repo; and it was not even the mechanism the _analyzer fix used.\n\nCURRENT RESIDUAL (whole-repo self-analysis, PR #640): 12 workspace-prefixed external_symbol phantoms = 8 documented carve-outs (5 scip_pb2 + 3 dunders) + Category D x3 + Category E x1. WI-tanot Categories A and B are now fully resolved; the only statically-resolvable residual is Category D + E (both tracked on WI-tanot; D awaits its own bakeoff-gated fix, E is a carve-out candidate).\n\nSCOPE NOTE (no weasel words): this fix advances ONLY the WI-tanot call/attr module_attr_ref facet. INV-nuzas's DOMINANT unfixed part — the tier classifier mis-tiering 168 hypergumbo_* modules and 366 imports edges mis-routed to phantom external twins (the resolver/classifier layer, per the 2026-05-30 note) — is UNTOUCHED by this PR. INV-nuzas stays `violated`; closure remains human-gated on the acceptance-property re-scope (after D/E land) AND the resolver/classifier fix."  # 78d0
