  message: "TIER-CLASSIFIER FACET ADVANCED (PR #655, dev @ 830f8bd426). Fixed the invariant clause \"Workspace dependency declarations should be internal-dependency\": _classify_symbols (cli.py) stamped every kind=dependency symbol tier-3 external unconditionally, so monorepo sibling declarations (hypergumbo-lang-common declaring hypergumbo-core; the meta-package declaring all siblings -- the normal path-dep pattern) were mis-tiered external, corrupting tier-weighted views (centrality, sketch first_party_priority). New supply_chain.collect_workspace_package_names(repo_root) reads every pyproject's [project].name / [tool.poetry].name (PEP503-normalized); a kind=dependency symbol whose name matches an in-repo package -> tier 2 internal_dep (\"workspace-internal dependency declaration\"). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (self-analysis before->after): the 9 hypergumbo-* sibling declarations flip external_dep->internal_dep (supply_chain_summary.internal_dep symbols 0->9, external_dep 1522->1513); the 67 genuine third-party declarations stay tier 3 (no over-promotion). Complements F3 (F3 fixed imported boundary nodes; this fixes dependency-declaration symbols) and realizes ADR-0041 sec.1 line-87's anticipated \"populate tier 2 with the workspace packages\" end-state.\n\nLIVE-MEASURED FACET STATE (self-analysis, this PR) -- the item history was internally contradictory about the \"dominant face\"; measured ground truth: import facet 366->0 (F3/F4, HOLDS -- the handoff's \"366-imports face untouched\" was a misread of PR #640's \"untouched by THIS PR\" scope note); boundary-node workspace mislabel (was 168) = 6 path='<external>' workspace phantoms; tier-classifier dependency-declaration facet NOW FIXED (9 -> tier 2). \n\nSTAYS violated: the WI-tanot call/attr phantom residual (6 workspace-prefix external_symbol phantoms = 3 dunder carve-outs + Category D cli.shutil/store.datetime + 1 NEW behavior_map_io.SubstrateError survey-rename-shim re-export) + the acceptance-property re-scope + close (human-gated per the 2026-07-08 ruling). \n\nPython pyproject-scoped; Cargo/npm sibling analogues are a documented follow-up (still tier 3). SPEC-RECONCILIATION NOTE (for human review): ADR-0041 sec.1's tier table (line 44 = \"monorepo siblings\") + line 87 AND this invariant clause both mandate tier 2 for sibling deps; the spec sec.14 \"sole tier-2 producer = internal_package_roots\" prose was the outlier (a gap for this case, not a deliberate exclusion) and was updated to name both producers. No schema/version bump (only tier VALUES change, not shapes)."  # e19a
