  nonce: '7333'  # 7333
  message: "SATISFIED (2026-07-15, human-approved re-scope). Closed on a RE-SCOPED acceptance property (the 2026-07-08 ruling's enumeration went stale; owner approved the re-scope this session).\n\nRE-SCOPED ACCEPTANCE PROPERTY (principle): No CONSUMER-VISIBLE external_symbol node carries a workspace-package prefix. A workspace-prefixed phantom is acceptable iff (a) statically invisible (no in-tree definition to resolve to), or (b) reachable ONLY from test files or build/CI scripts (consumer views filter test-reached nodes, so no consumer-facing surface sees it). Rationale: INV-nuzas's stated consequence is corruption of CONSUMER-FACING views (tier-weighting, slice, dead-code, import-walking); a test/script-only phantom never enters those, so consumer harm = 0. Self-maintaining: a future workspace-prefixed phantom is auto-acceptable only while test/script-reached; a consumer-reached one re-violates.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (production-path; closure-evidence discipline). `hypergumbo survey .` (dev @ 830f8bd426) -> predicate-exact acceptance measurement -> exactly 7 workspace-prefixed external_symbol nodes, EACH edge-source verified:\n  1-3. hypergumbo_core.__file__ / .__path__ / linkers.__path__ -- class (a) package dunders (import-time module_attr_ref).\n  4. hypergumbo_core.cli.shutil <- test_cli_symbols.py (test) -- class (b).\n  5. hypergumbo_tracker.store.datetime <- test_tui_snapshots.py (test) -- class (b).\n  6. hypergumbo_core.behavior_map_io.SubstrateError <- test_survey_io.py (test) -- class (b); survey-rename shim re-export, SELF-CLEARS at WI-sudin (deprecation-window close).\n  7. bash:hypergumbo <- scripts/dev-install + scripts/integration-test (build/CI scripts) -- class (b); a bash script's ref to the CLI is genuinely external (the \"hypergumbo\" match is the command name, not an in-tree Python module).\nAll 7 are class (a) or (b) => the re-scoped property HOLDS.\n\nCORRECTIONS vs the 2026-07-08 ruling's carve-out list (\"5 scip_pb2 + 3 dunders\"): the 5 scip_pb2 nodes no longer carry a workspace prefix (name=scip_pb2.Document) -> they already PASS, no carve needed. bash:hypergumbo (miscounted earlier under a hypergumbo_-with-underscore filter) and the new behavior_map_io.SubstrateError shim phantom are the two that actually fail; both class (b).\n\nFACETS CLOSED: imports mis-routed 366->0 (F3/F4, bakeoff-confirmed 2026-07-04); boundary-node tier mislabel 168->6; Categories A/B call/attr phantoms resolved; workspace-sibling DEPENDENCY-DECLARATION tier facet fixed (PR #655: 9 sibling declarations external_dep->internal_dep, 0 third-party over-promoted).\n\nNOT CLAIMED / ORTHOGONAL: the tier-axis concept-audit leaks (INV-higop F2 internal_dep semantic split, INV-bonup F3 tier-2 synthetic-node sentinel) are a SEPARATE outcome, unrelated to phantom naming. DOCUMENTED RESIDUAL (not a violation): the 4 test/script-reached carve-outs stay live phantoms in the raw graph; #6 self-clears at WI-sudin; #4/#5/#7 optionally fixable via WI-tanot (Cat-D relabel + a Cat-E bridge) but zero consumer harm and shared-emitter risk, so downgraded to optional cleanup."  # 7333
