  message: "STATEMENT REWORDED 2026-10-25, owner-approved, following the owner's ruling (option A, project frame) on the 2026-07-15 supply_chain_tier concept audit's finding F1. OLD clause: 'Workspace dependency declarations should be internal-dependency.' NEW clause: a dependency declaration naming an in-tree workspace package carries that package's tier (first-party), because every node standing for one package carries one tier. The old clause encoded the tier-2 reading ADR-0041 §1 is being rewritten to rule out: measuring a declaration from the member that declares it is the declaration-influences-tier pattern ADR-0041 exists to remove. STATUS: stays satisfied on its re-scoped acceptance property (2026-07-15: no consumer-visible external_symbol carries a workspace-package prefix), which is unchanged. The reworded declaration clause is NOT satisfied today and is carried as its own violated invariant, INV-kutub (python sibling declarations tier 2; npm/cargo sibling declarations and the js_module stand-in package node tier 3 'external', reproduced 2026-10-25 via hypergumbo survey on three workspace fixtures). The ADR/spec rewrite is WI-sufon."  # f4fd
