  message: "RE-OPENED 2026-10-25 (owner-approved), P1 -> P2, on positive evidence against the 2026-07-15 re-scoped acceptance property, whose own rule is 'a consumer-reached one re-violates'. Counterexamples, production `hypergumbo survey` on dev 9245df71d6: (1) PYTHON, reproduced independently by the orchestrator: a uv workspace where pkg-a's app.py does `import pkg_b.sub.deep; pkg_b.sub.deep.deep_fn()` calls `python:pkg_b.sub.deep:0-0:deep_fn:external_symbol` (path '<external>') although deep_fn is defined in packages/pkg-b; `from pkg_b.sub import deep; deep.deep_fn()` resolves; a single-package control fails the same way, so it is a general python dotted-module gap -- filed WI-lovun (P2). Same fixture: production-reached `pkg_b.REGISTRY.get()` / `pkg_b.core.CONSTANTS.values()` stubs, the Category-D shape the closure accepted only as test-reached (carve-out (a)'s wording is ambiguous for builtin methods; decided on WI-lovun). (2) JS AND CARGO: sibling-package imports call tier-3 phantoms (javascript:@ws/b:0-0:helper, rust:crate_b::helper:0-0:module external_symbols) instead of the sibling's source -- filed WI-rilof (P2). STATEMENT: the declaration clause added earlier today ('a declaration naming an in-tree workspace package carries that package's tier') is removed from this statement and lives on INV-kutub alone, so this item's status can never again assert a clause it knows is false; sentence 1 (packages/*/src is tier 1) holds; the path/prefix clause is the one now violated. Closes satisfied when WI-lovun and WI-rilof land and the property is re-checked on python, npm and cargo workspace fixtures. The description's Invariant / Candidate-fixes sections still say declarations 'should be internal_dep' -- superseded by the 2026-10-25 project-frame ruling (ADR-0041 §1, WI-sufon)."  # 18df
