  message: "RE-CHECK 2026-10-27 (the closure check this item's 10-25 reopen names: WI-lovun and WI-rilof landed, re-check on python, npm and cargo workspace fixtures). Production `hypergumbo survey` on merged dev 8c61dbe07c; fixtures and checker in the session scratchpad (nuzas_recheck/). STAYS VIOLATED: the filed shapes are fixed, but each ecosystem still has consumer-reached workspace-prefixed phantoms that have an in-tree definition.\n\nSentence 1 HOLDS on all four surveys: every node of workspace-package source is tier 1 (py fixture 21/21, npm 27/27, cargo 14/14; self-analysis 12,485 tier 1, plus 162 tier 3 that are all vendored tree-sitter grammars under hypergumbo_core/vendor/, reason 'in vendor/', correctly third-party).\n\nThe filed shapes RESOLVE (WI-lovun, WI-rilof re-run inside the fixtures): python `import pkg_b.sub.deep; pkg_b.sub.deep.deep_fn()`, `deep.deep_fn()`, `pkg_b.core.helper()` and both from-import spellings land on the real nodes; npm `const { helper } = require('@ws/b'); helper()` and ESM `import { shout } from '@ws/c'`; cargo `use crate_b::helper; helper()` and `crate_b::helper()`.\n\nCounterexamples (production source, in-tree definition exists), each with a control that resolves:\n1. PYTHON, flat-layout member (packages/pkg-c/pkg_c/, no src/): `import pkg_c`, `pkg_c.tools.shout()`, `pkg_c.tools.Loud().go()`, and `from pkg_c import tools` inside the member's own __init__ call python:pkg_c:... phantoms. Cause, read in code: _detect_source_roots (py.py:2480) only collects directories named src. Control: the same package at a repo root resolves. Filed WI-homih (P2).\n2. NPM, three shapes WI-rilof did not cover: `const b = require('@ws/b'); b.helper()`, `import * as C from '@ws/c'; C.shout()`, `import cDefault from '@ws/c'; cDefault()` call @ws/ phantoms. Control: the same shapes through relative imports resolve. Two general (relative-import) stand-ins also carry the @ws/ prefix and are left for that item to rule on: a module_attr_ref beside the correct instantiates edge for `new b.Engine()`, and the `<spec>:0-0:module` stand-in beside every real file import edge. Filed WI-halol (P2).\n3. CARGO, an aliased use: `use crate_b::{Thing, helper as h2}; h2()` calls rust:crate_b:0-0:helper. General Rust gap (in one crate `use crate::m::helper as h3; h3()` misses too); noted on WI-silam, which owns aliased uses.\nWI-homih, WI-halol and WI-silam now block this item.\n\nSELF-ANALYSIS (`hypergumbo survey .`, 5m53s): 29 workspace-prefixed external_symbol nodes (2026-07-15: 7), 23 reached only from tests/ or scripts/ (carve-out b). The 6 with a production source: scip_pb2.Index from rust_analyzer/translate.py and hypergumbo_tracker.__file__ from tracker/setup.py (carve-out a: generated protobuf class and package dunder, both accepted 07-15); SymbolsAt.get from llvm_ir.py:358 (carve-out a: SymbolsAt is a type alias of Dict, so get is dict.get with no in-tree definition, though the stub's module names the alias rather than builtins.dict); and the three console-script targets (hypergumbo_core.cli:main, hypergumbo_tracker.cli:main / textconv_main), now reached by defines_target edges from packages/*/pyproject.toml where 07-15 found them orphaned. These are WI-lipal's phantoms. Carve-out (b) covers them only if a build manifest counts as a 'build script'. I have not ruled on that reading; WI-lipal is open either way.\n\nCloses satisfied when WI-homih, WI-halol and WI-silam land and these fixtures re-run clean."  # d79d
- op: update  # 5056
  at: '2026-10-30T03:18:50Z'  # 5056
  by: agent  # 5056
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5056
  clock: 31  # 5056
  nonce: '5056'  # 5056
  set:  # 5056
    title: "Workspace code reached from another package (or its own manifest) lands on an external stand-in named by the in-tree module, not on the in-tree node"  # 5056
    description: "CURRENT STATE (re-checked 2026-10-29, merged dev 408f5950e9). The history is in the discussion; this section is what holds now.\n\nWHAT IS STILL WRONG. Code in one workspace package that reaches code in another package (or its own, through a manifest) sometimes lands on an external_symbol STAND-IN named by the in-tree module (python:pkg_c:0-0:pkg_c.tools, javascript:@ws/b:0-0:helper, rust:crate_b:0-0:helper), path '<external>', tier 3, instead of on the real in-tree node. In-tree code then reads as external in every consumer that walks those edges (slice, dead-code, entrypoints, tier-weighted views), and the real node misses its inbound edge.\n\nWHAT HOLDS. Tiering is NOT the defect any more: every node of workspace-package source is tier 1 on the python, npm and cargo fixtures (21/21, 27/27, 14/14) and on the self-map. The May 2026 symptoms are all fixed: 366 imports edges to stand-ins -> 0 (supply-verdict F3/F4), 144 hypergumbo_* modules tier-2 'direct dependency' -> 0, workspace sibling declarations tiered by the package they name (INV-kutub, satisfied). The shapes WI-lovun and WI-rilof fixed still resolve.\n\nACCEPTANCE PROPERTY (owner-approved re-scope, 2026-07-15). No consumer-reached external_symbol carries a workspace-package prefix. A workspace-prefixed stand-in is accepted only if (a) nothing in-tree defines it statically (a protobuf class built at import, a package dunder, a builtin method on a type alias such as SymbolsAt.get), or (b) it is reached only from test files or build/CI scripts. A pyproject.toml [project.scripts] entry is NOT a build script: it declares a production entry point.\n\nOPEN COUNTEREXAMPLES, each blocking this item:\n- WI-homih (P2) python: a workspace member with no src/ (packages/pkg-c/pkg_c/) is not a source root; _detect_source_roots collects only directories named src.\n- WI-halol (P2) js/ts: a sibling reached through a module object (const b = require('@ws/b'); b.helper()), a namespace import (import * as C) or a default import.\n- WI-silam (P3) rust: an aliased use (use crate_b::{Thing, helper as h2}; h2()).\n- WI-lipal (P3) python console scripts: on a src/ layout or across packages the build-target linker never finds the target file (target_path 'hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py' joined to the manifest dir misses src/), so the stand-in is the entry's only target. Self-map: hypergumbo_core.cli:main, hypergumbo_tracker.cli:main, hypergumbo_tracker.cli:textconv_main.\n\nSELF-MAP (2026-10-29, unchanged from 10-27): 29 workspace-prefixed external_symbol nodes; 23 reached only from tests/ or scripts/ (carve-out b); 6 with a production source = 3 carve-out (a) (scip_pb2.Index, hypergumbo_tracker.__file__, SymbolsAt.get) + the 3 WI-lipal console-script targets.\n\nCLOSES satisfied when WI-homih, WI-halol, WI-silam and WI-lipal land and the re-run is clean: fixtures, checker and the exact commands in ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nuzas_10292026/fixtures/README.md; self-map checker ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nuzas_10292026/self_check.py (expect 0 PROD rows outside carve-out a).\n\nNOT THIS ITEM. A dependency DECLARATION's tier is INV-kutub. The stdlib-through-a-module relabel and the bash `hypergumbo` command (test/script-reached) are optional cleanup on WI-tanot."  # 5056
    fields:  # 5056
      root_cause: "Resolution, not tiering. When an analyzer or linker cannot resolve a reference into a workspace package to its in-tree node, it emits an external_symbol stand-in named by that module (path <external>, tier 3), so in-tree code is represented as external. The tier classifier tiers what it is given correctly: workspace source is tier 1 and a stand-in is tier 3. Open resolution gaps: python flat-layout members are not source roots (WI-homih); js/ts module-object, namespace and default imports of a sibling (WI-halol); rust aliased use (WI-silam); pyproject console-script targets on a src/ layout or in another package (WI-lipal)."  # 5056
