  message: "PREMISE RE-CHECK 2026-10-29 (merged dev 408f5950e9; 27 commits since the 10-27 re-check, including INV-tugim python import resolution and the five META-mino resolution PRs). STAYS VIOLATED.\n\nMEASURED. Production hypergumbo survey on the 8 workspace fixtures and the self-map. Fixtures: edge and node sets identical to 10-27 apart from one unrelated python 'uses' edge to an HTTP call site; same counterexamples (py: 4 pkg_c stand-ins, WI-homih; js: 3, WI-halol; cargo: 1, WI-silam); controls still resolve; workspace source tier 1 (21/21, 27/27, 14/14). Self-map: the same 29 workspace-prefixed external_symbol nodes as 10-27, the same 6 with a production source.\n\nCORRECTED IN THE RECORD.\n1. TITLE and ROOT_CAUSE named the tier classifier. Measured wrong since 07-15 and again today: tiering is right (workspace source tier 1, stand-ins tier 3); the defect is resolution emitting a stand-in. Both rewritten; the 05-30 note already put the cause at the resolver.\n2. DESCRIPTION still carried the May symptoms (all fixed), an Invariant section saying declarations should be internal_dep (superseded 10-25 by the project-frame ruling, INV-kutub) and candidate fixes that have shipped. Replaced with the current state; the original text is in the item's history.\n3. The 10-27 note left the 3 console-script stand-ins unruled (is a build manifest a 'build script'?). Decided: a [project.scripts] entry declares a production entry point, it is not a build script, and on this repository the real functions get NO edge from the manifest at all (premise correction on WI-lipal). Outside both carve-outs; WI-lipal now blocks this item.\n4. The 10-27 fixtures lived in a session scratchpad and would not outlive it. Copied with the checker, a self-map checker and the exact re-run commands to ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nuzas_10292026/.\n\nNOT CHANGED. The statement (still true to the measured state), P2, status. Closure: WI-homih, WI-halol, WI-silam and WI-lipal land, then the README's re-run is clean.\n\nALSO STALE, NOT EDITED HERE: docs/adr/0041-supply-tier-purity.md lines 27 and 115 cite this item as 'P1, violated' under its old title."  # e946
- op: discuss  # a7d6
  at: '2026-10-30T04:48:14Z'  # a7d6
  by: agent  # a7d6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a7d6
  clock: 33  # a7d6
  nonce: a7d6  # a7d6
  message: "ACCEPTANCE PROPERTY, CARVE-OUT (c), decided 2026-10-30 on the owner's instruction to investigate the WI-lipal collision with ADR-0057 and decide (full reasoning on WI-lipal). A workspace-prefixed external_symbol is also accepted when every edge reaching it from production code is a stub that a STATED supersession demoted (meta superseded_by naming a resolved edge to the in-tree node, ADR-0057 section 14.1). Rationale: the statement forbids first-party symbols COLLAPSING to a placeholder; with a stated supersession the first-party symbol keeps its real path and is reached, and the placeholder carries a positive claim that names it. Carve-outs (a) and (b) of 2026-07-15 are unchanged. This does not assert that consumers counting external nodes read superseded_by. Closure check adds: each such stand-in's production in-edges all carry superseded_by."  # a7d6
